{%- comment -%}
  Line-item remove control.

  Deliberately NOT the same glyph as `drawer-close`. Both controls sit within a
  few pixels of each other in the cart drawer, and until #764 they rendered the
  identical 24x24 path, so "remove this line" and "close the drawer" were
  visually indistinguishable. A bin reads as destructive; the X stays reserved
  for dismissal.

  Decorative: every caller wraps this in a control that carries its own
  aria-label, so the icon is hidden from assistive tech.
{%- endcomment -%}
